  "id": "anycubic-kobra3",
  "name": "Anycubic Kobra 3 series toolhead (Kobra 3 / 3 Combo / 3 Max / 3 V2)",
  "provenance": "Anycubic Kobra 3 series toolhead (Kobra 3 / 3 Combo / 3 Max / 3 V2) Confidence: medium. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/1135683 (Anycubic Kobra 3 hotend STEP: nozzle, sock/heater block, heatsink, quick-release ears); https://www.printables.com/model/1326316 (Kobra 3 Toolhead Injection Molded Mid Frame, reverse engineered STEP, 73 x 53.4 x 97.5 mm); https://www.printables.com/model/1323789 (Kobra 3 Toolhead Fan Cover, reverse engineered STEP, 61 x 81 x 15.4 mm); https://www.printables.com/model/1266905 (Kobra 3 fan duct improved 3 ways, STEP remix of the stock duct); https://www.printables.com/model/1554516 (Kobra 3 cooling shroud upgrade: 'extends down past the edge of the heater block', so stock duct does not); https://www.printables.com/model/1467897 (Kobra 3 Ultimate shroud, stock-derived variant 2); https://www.printables.com/model/1550759 (Kobra 3 Combo V1 replacement duct); https://store.anycubic.com/products/hotend-module (Kobra 3 printhead assembly photo S010240); https://store.anycubic.com/products/cooling-fan (Kobra 3: 5020 dual-intake model blower, 3010 duct/hotend fan). Frame: nozzle tip at origin, +Y toward printer back. Nozzle and sock/heater block measured from the Kobra 3 hotend STEP (printables 1135683). Profile: tip flat r0.55, 30 deg cone to r1.5 at z1.75, hex to z2.75, flange/sock lip r5.75 from z2.75 to 3.75, then a 15.4 x 23.4 mm sock/heater block from z3.75 to about z26. The block's Y extent is -9.7..+13.7 around the nozzle, with the sign relative to the printer unknown, so it is enclosed by the duct level on both sides. Duct geometry comes from the stock-derived duct remixes (1266905, 1467897, 1554516, 1550759), which agree on a plenum about 56 W x 22-23 D x 37-41 H fed from above by the 5020 blower behind the front fan cover, and two legs 18-21 mm tall flanking the heater block with inner gap 20-25 mm. The 3-way remix lengthens the legs 'to improve ventilation in the back of the models', which puts the legs behind the plenum. The plenum's rear face is placed 11 mm in front of the nozzle (block half-depth 9.7 plus clearance), giving y -35.5..-11 for the plenum and -11..+14 for the legs, with 0.3 margins. 1554516 says its shroud 'extends down past the edge of the heater block', so the stock duct underside is at or above the block underside (z3.75), and z3.5 is used. The store photo of the head (S010240) shows the nozzle hidden behind the grey front lip of the shell, so the shell bottom is placed just above the duct at z4.0 and conservatively given the full 73 mm mid-frame width. The nozzle is placed about 30 mm behind the mid-frame front face (11 mm behind the 23 mm duct plenum), leaving 23.4 mm of frame behind it. The carriage and strain-gauge parts behind it are estimated out to +36. Kobra 3 Max uses the same printhead family. Kobra 3 V2 uses a revised hotend (separate store SKU) with a similar short exposed nozzle, and these levels are applied to it unchanged. [1] Footnote: the mid frame, fan cover and hotend are community reverse-engineered models, not Anycubic CAD. Duct, shell and gantry placement relative to the tip are derived/estimated (about +-1 mm). The gantry (X extrusion behind the carriage) at z35, y30..56 is an estimate from head proportions. parts: per-component boxes with no 0.3 margin. Duct and shell are extended downward by uncertainty (duct underside 3.5, shell 3.8). Mid-frame y0 is placed at printer y=-30. Nozzle: land radius 0.55 mm, 30.0-degree cone to Z=1.75, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 35.00 mm above the tip, Y 30.0..56.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/anycubic-kobra3.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
